WEBVTT

00:04.760 --> 00:06.930
That explosion came from inside the tower!

00:06.930 --> 00:08.740
The only ones capable of that are...

00:09.740 --> 00:13.240
Those infuriating, aberrant monsters...

00:13.620 --> 00:15.270
The Magia Vander!

00:31.010 --> 00:35.720
Episode 24
A Story of a Dream with No End

01:50.010 --> 01:52.120
W-We're alive.

01:52.120 --> 01:54.260
I thought we were gonna die.

01:54.260 --> 01:55.510
Elfie!

02:02.660 --> 02:04.310
A draw, huh?

02:04.660 --> 02:07.060
I guess you <i>can</i> fight, wench!

02:07.060 --> 02:09.440
I could say the same to you!

02:09.440 --> 02:12.940
That ate up all my magical energy.

02:12.940 --> 02:16.070
But you're still ready to go, right?

02:16.070 --> 02:17.320
Of course.

02:18.700 --> 02:20.450
Then let's do this!

02:20.720 --> 02:22.580
I will not lose to you!

02:32.210 --> 02:33.720
That's enough.

02:37.220 --> 02:38.960
Please, move out of the way, Ellenor!

02:38.960 --> 02:41.140
You're out of time, halfwit.

02:41.140 --> 02:44.230
It would have been more convenient 
if you'd accidentally killed each other.

02:44.230 --> 02:46.230
Get lost, ratbag!

02:46.230 --> 02:48.180
I was kind enough to stand by and watch,

02:48.180 --> 02:51.910
but you two couldn't settle things, 
so this is on you, Zeo.

02:51.910 --> 02:52.660
Besides...

02:52.660 --> 02:53.490
Huh?

02:53.490 --> 02:57.370
When the sovereign speaks, 
even you will have to listen.

03:02.580 --> 03:04.500
<b>Magia Vander Masterias Noah
 Five Supreme Wands, Light Sovereign's Wand
Aaron Masterias Oldking</b>

03:02.620 --> 03:04.120
You will stop.

03:08.150 --> 03:13.130
I will not permit any further 
clashing between two Magia Vander.

03:13.130 --> 03:15.010
Don't interfere, geezer!

03:15.010 --> 03:19.300
No amount of intercession will work! 
Not unless Will's place is decided!

03:19.300 --> 03:23.350
And there's no way to decide this 
other than a fight, right?!

03:38.260 --> 03:40.030
Rock, paper, scissors.

03:41.370 --> 03:43.240
Rock, paper, scissors?

03:48.340 --> 03:51.460
Should you resort to any other method,

03:51.460 --> 03:55.510
then Will Serfort shall come 
under my command.

03:56.330 --> 03:58.760
First comes rock...

03:59.120 --> 03:59.760
Really?

03:59.760 --> 04:01.260
Damn it all.

04:01.970 --> 04:03.760
Let's go! Come on!

04:03.760 --> 04:05.640
I'm gonna win!

04:06.090 --> 04:08.610
Rock, paper, scissors!

04:08.610 --> 04:10.270
Again, to break the tie!

04:10.270 --> 04:15.050
Again, to break the tie!

04:15.050 --> 04:23.160
Again, to break the tie! Again, to break 
the tie! Again, to break the tie!

04:15.050 --> 04:19.180
Hey, Julius? Really, what's happening here?

04:19.180 --> 04:23.160
If we go back to the beginning, you're 
pretty much the root cause of all of this.

04:23.160 --> 04:28.670
Again, to break the tie!

04:29.990 --> 04:38.170
Again, to break the tie! Again, to break 
the tie! Again, to break the tie!

04:38.170 --> 04:39.430
Again, to break the tie!

04:39.430 --> 04:40.680
Again, to break the tie!

04:40.680 --> 04:43.690
Again, to break the tie!

04:40.680 --> 04:42.050
<b>299 throws, 299 ties</b>

04:44.890 --> 04:48.350
<b>300 throws, 299 ties</b>

04:51.350 --> 04:53.490
Yeah!

04:53.490 --> 04:55.360
Applaud him, Owenzaus!

04:55.360 --> 04:56.660
Yes, sir.

04:57.150 --> 04:59.110
<b>Zeo wins with rock</b>

04:59.110 --> 05:00.830
E-Elfie...

05:01.750 --> 05:05.880
Now you belong to me! 
And you don't get to complain!

05:05.880 --> 05:07.010
What?

05:07.010 --> 05:10.250
No! I hate this!
 I hate it, I hate it, I hate it!

05:10.250 --> 05:12.980
I'm staying with Will!

05:14.170 --> 05:18.100
Will! I don't want this!

05:18.100 --> 05:24.050
<i>That's right. Elfie had to leave me
and ascend the tower alone.</i>

05:24.050 --> 05:26.390
<i>She's waited for me 
for six years, and now...</i>

05:26.390 --> 05:29.300
I hate this! No!

05:26.920 --> 05:30.520
<i>The truth is that I want 
to stay with her too, but...</i>

05:31.900 --> 05:32.770
It's all right.

05:34.020 --> 05:35.420
We'll see each other again.

05:35.840 --> 05:37.930
No, I'll come and see you.

05:39.510 --> 05:41.080
Will...

05:41.080 --> 05:43.410
Come on. We're going.

05:43.410 --> 05:45.300
By Lord Aaron's command.

05:47.660 --> 05:49.270
What? Wait! I can't!

05:49.170 --> 05:54.320
Please don't embarrass 
yourself any further, Lady Elfaria!

05:49.270 --> 05:50.810
I can't do this! I can't, I can't!

05:50.810 --> 05:53.080
No! I hate this! No!

05:53.080 --> 05:55.170
Let go of me! Will!

05:55.170 --> 05:59.420
Will!

06:01.400 --> 06:03.640
Looks like you understand how things work.

06:03.640 --> 06:06.140
I thought you were gonna
go berserk like a wild animal.

06:07.090 --> 06:12.100
If I say anything selfish, 
Elfie will fight and get hurt again.

06:12.790 --> 06:13.770
Which is why...

06:14.450 --> 06:16.580
Will you promise me something?

06:16.580 --> 06:19.020
Promise you won't fight 
with Elfie anymore.

06:19.600 --> 06:25.780
If you don't promise me that, 
I'll defeat you and run to her!

06:33.940 --> 06:37.290
I like that cocky grit of yours! 
That's just my style.

06:51.220 --> 06:54.450
Starting today, you're part 
of the lightning faction.

07:04.360 --> 07:07.950
I show no mercy. Better prepare yourself!

07:09.120 --> 07:09.910
Yes, sir!

07:12.700 --> 07:16.000
<b><u>Prime Magic</u>

Every mage dreams at least once of achieving the pinnacle
 of each magical affinity. Prime magic is precisely that. As it
 demands every spellwork technique and powerful magical energy,
 if you acquire it, at the very least, your admittance to a faction 
in the tower is assured. It functions as authority itself. Then
 prime magic must be the ultimate height of magic, you say?
 Fool. You are utterly hopeless. The path of magic boasts even 
greater heights.

-Edward Serfence</b>

07:17.710 --> 07:21.000
<b><u>The Grim Generation</u>

All of you budding mages have finished the First Bloom. 
It isn't just Will and his friends now. All of you will
 enter into a phase of tremendous growth. 
And we would like to call that hope.
May you reach the heavens and defeat all evil.

-Cerridwen</b>

07:21.660 --> 07:25.260
And now, we of the 401st class, 
the Grim Generation...

07:25.260 --> 07:29.510
have all been accepted 
into factions! Congratulations!

07:25.510 --> 07:29.510
<b>Clairie's House
Secret Base for Single Witches</b>

07:29.510 --> 07:31.140
Cheers!

07:31.140 --> 07:33.640
Cheers!

07:33.640 --> 07:35.020
Cheers!

07:35.990 --> 07:40.150
Hey! Do you honestly think it's all right 
to fool around like this in the tower?

07:40.150 --> 07:41.970
What's it going to hurt, Emma?

07:41.970 --> 07:45.850
They told us we're free to do whatever 
until our guidance session tomorrow.

07:45.850 --> 07:48.730
We're all in different factions now.

07:48.730 --> 07:50.720
I don't know about
 fraternizing with rivals.

07:50.720 --> 07:54.040
Now, now, Miss Emma, 
my dear model student...

07:54.040 --> 08:00.250
You're actually so happy 
you could jump for joy, aren't you?

08:00.830 --> 08:01.710
I...

08:01.710 --> 08:03.230
I'm over the moon!

08:03.230 --> 08:05.130
You actually wanna
be celebrated, don't you?

08:05.130 --> 08:07.080
I want to be celebrated!

08:07.080 --> 08:08.260
Then it's time to party!

08:08.260 --> 08:14.260
Now, to the one who dragged us leftovers
with her! To Emma! Another toast!

08:14.260 --> 08:15.640
Ready, and...

08:15.640 --> 08:18.140
Cheers!

08:18.140 --> 08:20.270
Cheers!

08:32.470 --> 08:33.560
Lihanna?

08:33.560 --> 08:34.540
Are you all right?

08:36.430 --> 08:39.700
Apologies. The exhaustion 
of the last few days has...

08:40.500 --> 08:45.300
Will, you'll understand soon enough now 
that you've joined the lightning faction.

08:45.660 --> 08:49.360
You've got me super curious, 
if also a little bit scared.

08:49.360 --> 08:50.300
Want to eat?

08:51.200 --> 08:52.460
I do.

08:56.930 --> 09:00.680
Everything's a mess because you
went and joined the lightning faction.

09:00.680 --> 09:01.310
What?

09:01.860 --> 09:04.780
Lady Elfaria kept crying, 
and when I tried to comfort her,

09:04.780 --> 09:08.820
she yelled, "I quit everything!" 
Then she tried to run away!

09:08.820 --> 09:13.070
We all had to stop Lady Elfaria after
you left things like that, and then you—

09:13.070 --> 09:15.420
I-I'm really sorry!

09:19.830 --> 09:21.200
You forgot these.

09:21.200 --> 09:22.330
Take them with you.

09:23.040 --> 09:24.790
Thank you, Julius!

09:24.790 --> 09:26.090
Hey!

09:26.090 --> 09:28.990
Are you two getting along 
even better than you did before?

09:28.990 --> 09:31.750
Colette, why are you angry?

09:31.750 --> 09:34.090
I-I'm not angry.

09:34.480 --> 09:36.790
Colette is envious.

09:36.790 --> 09:41.100
You forged a deep bond while she wasn't
looking, so she's jealous of Julius.

09:41.100 --> 09:42.220
W-Wignall!

09:42.220 --> 09:44.650
I never forged any bonds!

09:44.960 --> 09:48.900
I have no intention of joining your 
game of playing friends, understand?

09:48.900 --> 09:51.650
What do you mean, "playing friends"?!

09:51.650 --> 09:54.030
Honestly. He only ever says mean things.

09:54.030 --> 09:58.660
I think I've started to understand his
breed of kindness a little better, though.

09:58.660 --> 10:00.310
Hey, book-learner!

10:00.310 --> 10:01.790
We've been looking for you!

10:02.250 --> 10:05.550
You should get out here. You're part 
of our comeback club, aren't you?

10:05.550 --> 10:07.670
What? Um...

10:07.670 --> 10:09.170
You should go.

10:09.170 --> 10:11.420
You're worthy of far more
recognition than you receive.

10:12.270 --> 10:13.580
Thank you.

10:13.580 --> 10:14.680
I'll be back!

10:16.420 --> 10:18.660
Everyone wants to talk to you.

10:18.660 --> 10:19.430
What?

10:19.430 --> 10:21.180
Just how did you...

10:24.200 --> 10:27.200
It's exactly like Emma said.

10:27.200 --> 10:29.940
I can't keep Will all to myself anymore.

10:30.910 --> 10:32.340
Colette?

10:32.340 --> 10:34.410
I just feel lonely.

10:34.830 --> 10:38.410
I'm not his only friend any longer.

10:39.540 --> 10:42.300
I'm selfish... and annoying.

10:42.770 --> 10:45.170
I haven't changed at all 
from who I was before.

10:46.000 --> 10:48.140
Nothing will come of self-deprecation.

10:49.210 --> 10:51.610
I've decided to stop waiting.

10:51.610 --> 10:53.090
Wignall...

10:53.090 --> 10:55.590
I don't mean that I've given up.

10:55.590 --> 11:00.010
I will use my own strength 
to get closer to the person I seek.

11:00.800 --> 11:02.450
Will taught me that.

11:03.490 --> 11:06.230
When a coward fears running away...

11:06.920 --> 11:10.110
That's called courage, isn't it, Colette?

11:12.200 --> 11:16.500
I'm a selfish, annoying woman...

11:19.330 --> 11:21.870
but there's something I want to tell Will!

11:21.870 --> 11:23.660
Then you should go.

11:25.390 --> 11:26.380
Right.

11:37.220 --> 11:39.990
Should we help her?

11:39.990 --> 11:41.910
Let's watch over her a bit longer.

11:48.090 --> 11:49.860
Why are you acting so melancholy?

11:50.810 --> 11:54.080
Are you lonely now that
you've got no one to bully?

11:54.780 --> 11:57.430
You are a stubborn, spiteful Ulster.

11:57.430 --> 12:00.510
The truth is that you want 
to tyrannize him more, right?

12:05.440 --> 12:08.370
There's no longer any need for that.

12:09.120 --> 12:10.380
He isn't pathetic anymore.

12:10.960 --> 12:14.420
He's infuriating, but it doesn't 
offend me to look at him now.

12:15.130 --> 12:17.210
I never imagined this day would come.

12:17.980 --> 12:18.760
Sion!

12:19.410 --> 12:21.440
You never let me say it before,

12:21.440 --> 12:23.770
but about Terminalia,
 the graduation ceremony,

12:23.770 --> 12:25.220
and so much else... Thank you!

12:27.330 --> 12:28.970
So, um...

12:28.970 --> 12:31.810
would it be all right for me 
to come up to where you are?

12:31.810 --> 12:32.900
For what purpose?

12:32.900 --> 12:36.650
What? Um, well... to thank you?

12:36.650 --> 12:37.530
In that case...

12:37.970 --> 12:39.780
fight me.

12:39.780 --> 12:41.030
What?

12:46.040 --> 12:49.040
It's the perfect gesture in lieu 
of thanks, wouldn't you say?

12:49.040 --> 12:50.240
A fine idea.

12:50.240 --> 12:51.670
Let me join in!

12:55.600 --> 12:58.000
With this, I forgive what 
you owe me for training you.

12:58.000 --> 12:59.300
What? Wait!

13:00.830 --> 13:03.550
Go. Go now, Colette Loire.

13:04.700 --> 13:05.550
All right!

13:06.440 --> 13:07.440
Will!

13:08.060 --> 13:09.680
There's something I want to tell you!

13:09.680 --> 13:11.810
Go!

13:11.810 --> 13:12.560
Huh?

13:21.570 --> 13:24.030
You're not going, Iris?

13:24.470 --> 13:27.540
Even if I did, it would only 
confuse everyone.

13:27.540 --> 13:32.540
Besides, it would expose 
my true identity to Will.

13:32.540 --> 13:36.170
Watchers are always 
so secretive, aren't they?

13:37.140 --> 13:39.670
I think that's the wrong move, though.

13:40.700 --> 13:43.380
If you get too fixated on maintaining
your underclassman image,

13:43.380 --> 13:45.930
someone else will steal 
him away, you know?

13:45.930 --> 13:48.120
Please don't just appear
whenever you feel like it!

13:48.120 --> 13:50.640
Also, I never asked for your advice.

13:50.640 --> 13:54.060
I'm rooting for you, Iris.

13:55.730 --> 13:58.190
Invess, please make me a promise.

13:58.190 --> 14:00.820
If you call me Finn, I might listen.

14:01.890 --> 14:02.820
Finn.

14:04.180 --> 14:07.450
Will has officially become
a member of the tower.

14:07.880 --> 14:13.080
So... please don't take him away just yet.

14:13.410 --> 14:14.960
Very well.

14:14.960 --> 14:19.460
I will respect Cerridwen's wishes 
and sit back a little while longer.

14:20.030 --> 14:23.730
However, should the sword fail 
to make good progress,

14:23.730 --> 14:25.970
I will take him,
and that's not up for discussion.

14:25.970 --> 14:27.470
Feel free to do so.

14:27.890 --> 14:31.350
All is done to transcend the heavens.

14:33.350 --> 14:35.350
Hey, all of you!

14:35.750 --> 14:38.480
Just what do you think you're doing?!

14:40.480 --> 14:44.610
You've ascended to the tower, 
yet you're still acting like students?

14:44.930 --> 14:47.510
You are sorely lacking
 in awareness as high mages!

14:48.030 --> 14:49.460
At least...

14:49.460 --> 14:52.370
that's how I would have 
scolded you not so long ago.

14:54.370 --> 14:56.510
Don't relax too much.

14:56.510 --> 14:59.880
I give that advice not as your teacher,
 but as a senior mage.

14:59.880 --> 15:01.880
Professor Workner...

15:02.740 --> 15:03.600
Will.

15:04.730 --> 15:06.260
Do you have a little time right now?

15:06.260 --> 15:07.220
What?

15:10.830 --> 15:14.650
Will, congratulations on making it 
through the Second Bloom!

15:14.650 --> 15:18.360
You congratulated me so many times 
after the graduation ceremony, too.

15:18.360 --> 15:20.650
You even cried more than I did.

15:20.650 --> 15:24.900
D-Don't poke fun at me, you blockhead! 
That's just what teachers are like!

15:24.900 --> 15:26.330
Honestly...

15:26.730 --> 15:28.280
Professor Workner?

15:29.050 --> 15:30.590
I have a request.

15:31.210 --> 15:32.290
What is it?

15:32.290 --> 15:35.240
Is there any way for me to see Elfie?

15:35.740 --> 15:38.790
I want to see her 
more than anything right now.

15:40.890 --> 15:44.720
For someone from a different faction, 
meeting a Magia Vander is impossible.

15:45.880 --> 15:51.210
But coincidentally, there's a certain 
female student who wants to see you, too.

15:51.210 --> 15:51.810
What?

15:51.810 --> 15:53.200
Go get changed!

15:53.200 --> 15:54.620
We're sneaking out of the tower!

15:54.620 --> 15:55.680
What?

15:59.650 --> 16:02.820
That Workner... He's taking 
his favoritism much too far.

16:02.820 --> 16:05.180
You mean his sweet little treat?

16:05.180 --> 16:08.300
It's because a different teacher, 
one as terrifying as a snake,

16:08.300 --> 16:11.700
rained down the lashings
nearly to his breaking point, you know?

16:13.600 --> 16:17.850
Ah, youth! It's just like back in our day!

16:19.420 --> 16:21.620
I'll come back for you at twelve.

16:21.620 --> 16:24.090
Until then, make sure 
you can leave without regrets.

16:25.710 --> 16:26.570
Hup!

16:34.370 --> 16:35.390
Elfie!

16:37.730 --> 16:38.730
Will!

16:39.160 --> 16:40.470
I'm sorry it took me so long—

16:42.230 --> 16:48.280
Why'd you go to Zeo?! Do you hate me now?!

16:48.280 --> 16:48.760
What?

16:48.760 --> 16:51.570
No! Elfie, you lost 
at rock, paper, scissors.

16:51.570 --> 16:54.240
I hate this! I hate it, I hate it!

16:54.240 --> 16:57.740
I thought I'd finally get 
to be with you, Will, and now...

16:57.740 --> 17:01.770
I don't want you to be 
Zeo's bride! I hate it!

17:01.770 --> 17:04.960
What do you mean, "bride"?! 
That's not going to happen!

17:06.670 --> 17:10.220
I wanted to be together too,
 but then I thought...

17:10.610 --> 17:13.210
"Are we really all right 
with this being the goal?"

17:13.210 --> 17:14.220
The goal?

17:15.150 --> 17:17.970
What was the promise we made?

17:18.330 --> 17:22.980
To become Magia Vander 
and go see the sunset.

17:22.980 --> 17:23.910
Exactly.

17:24.410 --> 17:27.320
I can't stand at your side yet, Elfie.

17:27.810 --> 17:29.650
That's why I want to get stronger.

17:30.080 --> 17:31.940
Even so, I hate this!

17:31.940 --> 17:32.610
What?!

17:33.250 --> 17:39.880
I want to be with you, Will. To touch you 
and feel your warmth. But this...

17:39.880 --> 17:41.750
You know, about that...

17:43.170 --> 17:47.250
A long time ago, didn't you go like this
 and try to play a trick on me?

17:47.250 --> 17:51.460
Wha—?! Wh-Wh-What sort of p-prank?

17:52.520 --> 17:53.910
Like a kiss or something?

17:53.910 --> 17:56.510
I-I-I-I-I have no idea 
what you're talking about!

17:57.000 --> 17:57.930
Really?

17:57.930 --> 18:01.520
R-Really! I'm not Colette, you know?

18:01.520 --> 18:04.010
Why bring up Colette now?

18:07.480 --> 18:08.900
So you remember that?

18:09.330 --> 18:14.780
Yes, but I feel like there are 
 things I don't remember yet.

18:15.140 --> 18:17.230
Cerridwen explained things to me.

18:17.230 --> 18:22.370
She said that I'll be able to move forward
by recalling paths of magic I've walked.

18:22.790 --> 18:26.730
Which is why if there's anything 
I've forgotten, I want it back.

18:26.730 --> 18:28.550
Including what we treasured, Elfie.

18:31.060 --> 18:33.050
You're so greedy, Will.

18:33.050 --> 18:36.300
That's right. Greedy enough 
to be a match for you.

18:36.300 --> 18:39.560
Really? In that case, I forgive you.

18:39.970 --> 18:41.310
But in exchange...

18:41.870 --> 18:43.910
let's go and take a peek at the sky!

18:50.940 --> 18:54.200
We can see it from much closer than 
we did when we made that promise!

18:58.290 --> 19:01.370
These stairs... People won't 
spot them, will they?

19:01.370 --> 19:04.500
I cast illusion magic on them. 
Don't worry.

19:04.500 --> 19:08.130
More importantly, we have to hurry
 before it's twelve!

19:08.130 --> 19:08.950
Yeah!

19:11.050 --> 19:14.980
Will, your back is so much bigger 
than it was back then.

19:14.980 --> 19:16.260
You think so?

19:16.720 --> 19:17.660
Yup.

19:18.090 --> 19:20.670
You're much, much bigger.

19:21.220 --> 19:22.310
But...

19:23.410 --> 19:25.230
your warmth hasn't changed at all.

19:33.730 --> 19:38.260
It's so beautiful, but this sky is fake,

19:38.670 --> 19:42.610
and the Celestial Host lurks beyond.

19:43.240 --> 19:44.080
Yup.

19:44.580 --> 19:47.080
The promise we made...

19:47.080 --> 19:51.000
It might just be the most difficult 
promise to keep in the whole world.

19:54.170 --> 19:55.260
But even if it is...

19:55.570 --> 19:57.570
Yeah, even if it is...

19:58.010 --> 19:59.450
It's a promise.

19:59.450 --> 20:03.430
Let's watch the sunset together,
 just you and me!

21:43.070 --> 21:45.990
<b>Wistoria: Wand and Sword</b>

21:49.040 --> 21:52.500
<b>Tower, 1st Floor: Temporary Quarters</b>

21:52.500 --> 21:55.570
I got too carried away yesterday.

21:55.570 --> 21:57.750
I ate and drank way too much. 
This is dire.

21:57.750 --> 22:01.010
I wonder what kinds of things 
they'll teach us in this guidance session.

22:01.320 --> 22:04.470
Probably tips about living here.

22:04.470 --> 22:06.060
There are factions, after all.

22:06.060 --> 22:10.520
Indeed, they do say that things are
different here than at the academy.

22:12.020 --> 22:18.020
Thanks for waiting! And congrats 
to all you graduates on joining factions!

22:18.440 --> 22:21.010
That's the Grim Generation for you!

22:21.010 --> 22:22.820
Even those who didn't make the First Bloom

22:22.820 --> 22:26.530
managed to turn the unknown 
into the known and receive blessings!

22:26.530 --> 22:30.660
As expected, all of your outstanding 
potential is shining brightly!

22:31.040 --> 22:36.670
So, in previous years, this is when
 I'd give you orientation about the tower...

22:36.670 --> 22:40.300
But for your class,
 I'm giving you a top secret order.

22:40.300 --> 22:41.300
What?

22:41.300 --> 22:45.470
Your mission is to spy 
on the factions you've joined.

22:45.470 --> 22:48.180
Conversations with fellow members,
their behavior and records...

22:48.180 --> 22:50.940
Should you find anything suspicious, 
investigate thoroughly

22:50.940 --> 22:52.120
and report back.

22:52.680 --> 22:54.690
Wh-What's all this about?

22:54.690 --> 22:59.240
The surprise attack at Terminalia
should still be fresh in all your minds.

22:59.240 --> 23:02.320
After investigating 
what lay behind the incident...

23:02.640 --> 23:06.820
all evidence pointed to just one thing.
Someone on the inside assisted them.

23:10.310 --> 23:11.580
It can't be...

23:11.580 --> 23:12.580
That's right.

23:12.580 --> 23:15.330
There is a traitor in the tower.

23:24.450 --> 23:26.030
A traitor?

